ShenDoragon: {
	Spawn: {
		First: {
			1: Surprised to see us again, Kid?
			2: NYEHEHEHEHEH..! Yes..! Must be shocking to see us here..! But this time, we have a little tricksie up our sleeves..!
			3: That Sigil you just used gave us back our full power, which will let us reach our true, powerful form..!
			4: We used to be the same being..! But then a Terrarian wretch like you split our soul in half..! But now...heheheh...
			5: WE ARE COMPLETE AGAIN
			6: Heh....heheh...
			7: You've made a grave mistake, child...
			8: For you see....
			9: I AM SHEN DORAGON, EMPEROR OF CHAOS AND ANARCHY!
			10: And you, my child...
			11: WILL PERISH!!!
		}
	}

	Summon: Grips! Assist me!

	Health: {
		80: {
			First: What's this? Competence? Impressive.
			Repeat: Quite the skill, kid.
		}

		66: {
			First: Chaos always reigns, kid. You terrarians never seem to learn that.
			Repeat: You're a real fighter, you know. Now stand still and let me grill you.
		}

		30: {
			First: Hmm...still fighting, eh?
			Repeat: Looks like you're turning tide, but not for long!
		}
	}

	Defeat: {
		NotExpert: {
			First: Heh, alright. I’ll leave you alone I guess. But if you come back stronger, I’ll show you the power of true unyielding chaos...
			Repeat: Good show, child, good show. Your combat prowess still impresses me! Maybe some day I'll show you my true power.
		}
	}

	Transition: {
		1: Heh...
		2: Heheheh...
		3: HAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!
		4: Have you forgotten about our last battles...?
		5: There's always a last stand, kiddo...
		6: But now, you stand in my path...
		7: Shen Doragon has been Awakened!
		8: YOU WILL BURN IN THE FLAMES OF DISCORDIAN HELL!!!
	}

	Awakened: {
		Summon: {
			First: {
				Shen: Girls..? Help your father with this insignificant mortal.
				Ashe: With pleasure, Papa~!
				Haruka: Yes, father.
			}

			Repeat: {
				Shen: Ashe? Haruka? I need your assistance again..!
				Ashe: On it, Papa~!
				Haruka: Again..?
			}

			Flee: {
				Ashe: AGH! Sorry papa..! I gotta bail!
				Haruka: Ngh...sorry father...I can't carry on...
			}
		}

		Health: {
			90: {
				First: Look at where you are, terrarian. This is your own doing. The ritual, the rune? All you.
				Repeat: You put up a real fight, kid.
			}

			80: {
				First: Why do you instigate all these fights? Power? Glory?
				Repeat: Brawlin' till the very end.
			}

			70: {
				First: Either way, I'll personally make sure this is your last one!
				Repeat: You remind me of myself quite a bit...
			}

			60: {
				First: How many times will you fight to tear me down? Or will you give up?
				Repeat: You're strong, too. Takes guts to fight most of what you have.
			}

			50: {
				Thorium: You know, I was watching you beat down that god-sphere and its 3 goons. Gotta admit, pretty impressive.
				CalamityMod: Considering you put that angsty witch in her place, gotta hand it to ya.
				GRealm: Seeing you squashed that oversided insect in the jungle, that's quite a head-turner.
				Redemption: However, after you walloped that cosmic prude, even I was taken aback by that level of skill.
				Jetshift: But slaying those two meteor-squatting crystal things? That's quite an eye-catcher.
				SpiritOld: Now that I think about it, though, you cracking open that overseer like an egg? Quite the strength that had to have needed.
				NoMod: Everything you've torn down, gods and monsters alike, I respect that.
				#New Additions
				SpiritClassic: Now that I think about it, though, you making that old sentinel crumble to pebbles? Quite the strength that had to have needed.
				StarsAbove: Though after you put down that rogue Starfarer, you really got my attention.
				LunarVeil: Looking back, I gotta give you credit for managing to quell that green goddess punk.
				SacredTools: Dousing that abyssal pumpkin? Now that was a sight to see!
				Catalyst: You really did wipe the floor with the purple pile of sludge.
				CalamityHunt: Must've taken a whole lot to put those slimes back in their place. Who'd have thought they could put up a fight!

				Split: {
					Seth: I'll admit, putting down that sword-slinging hothead was quite the show to witness.
					SethUltimate: I'll admit, putting down that sword-slinging hothead, with his true power unleashed, was quite the show to witness.
				}

				Macrocosm: You even took your fury to the Moon! Now that's something I can get behind.
				Spooky: Tearing through those catacombs like you own the place. That takes some skill.

				Ultranium: {
					Erebus: Watching you whallop that tentacle-covered worm? That was a treat!
					Aldin: Watching you whallop that star slinging hobo? That was a treat!
				}

				YouBoss: I mean, shattering your own reflection come alive? That's impressive stuff.
				Radiance: I didn't think that sun fairy was all too impressive until you managed to bring out her full power. That was a spectacle indeed!
			}

			30: {
				First: Hm..?! You haven't kicked the bucket yet? Well then...Let's change that!
				Repeat: Hmpf..! Here we are again, gettin' close to the end of the line. I'm not holding back!
			}

			20: {
				First: You little..! Die already!
				Repeat: The end of a game is the most stressful, keep that in mind, kid!
			}

			10: {
				First: This can't be--! How?!
				Repeat: This is it! The end is near, so don't you dare hold back!
			}
		}

		Defeat: {
			First: {
				1: Split again...
				2: This is YOUR fault you insolent worm..! I knew we should have been more aggressive but NOOOOOOOOO..! YOU said we could squash them without even trying!

				3: {
					Singleplayer: "{0}, you will face our fury again one day...either when we gain enough power again..."
					Multiplayer: Warriors, you will face our fury again one day...either when we gain enough power again...
				}

				4: ...or you decide to use that Sigil again..!
				5: Your choice, child.
			}

			Repeat: {
				1: YOU IMBECILE! WE LOST! AGAAAAAAAAAAAAIN!!!
				2: Rgh, my head...

				3: {
					Singleplayer: {
						Male: AND YOU, BOY! NEXT TIME I'M GONNA TEAR YOUR HEAD OFF!!!
						Female: AND YOU, GIRL! NEXT TIME I'M GONNA TEAR YOUR HEAD OFF!!!
					}

					Multiplayer: AND YOU BUNCH OF CLOWNS! NEXT TIME I'M GONNA TEAR YOUR HEADS OFF!!!
				}

				4: And trust us, kid.
				5: There's always a next time.
			}
		}
	}

	#Unused
	FuryAshe1: "Papa, NO! You'll PAY for this, "
	WrathHaruka1: Father! Rrgh..! Next time we meet, I'll strike you down!
	ShenDoragon1: TERRA MAGIC?! NO! I THOUGHT IT WAS WIPED FROM THE EARTH!
	ShenDoragon9: You are quite persistent, Child. I like that.
	ShenDoragon10: What's this? Competence? I would have never expected...
	ShenDoragon11: True warriors don't show mercy! I won't and I doubt you will either..!
	ShenDoragon12: Give up, child. The world will always fall into chaos!
	ShenDoragon13: SHOW NO MERCY!
	ShenDoragon14: What? You're still fighting? Why?!
	ShenDoragon15: The defeat of a superancient empowers the stonekeepers.
	ShenDoragon17: The defeat of a superancient empowers the stonekeepers.
}

InfinityZero: {
	Spawn: ...Target Identified.

	Health: {
		75: WARNING. Systems have reached 75% efficiency.
		50: Redirecting resources to offensive systems.
		25: CRITICAL WARNING. Systems have reached 25% efficiency. Failure imminent.
		10: Terrarian, you will not win this. Rerouting all resources to offensive systems.
	}

	Zeroes: {
		Revived: Zero Units sufficiently repaired. Reengaging Core defense system.
		Defeated: Zero Units in critical condition. Rerouting resources to repair systems. Core defense temporarily disabled.
	}

	Defeat: {
		First: {
			1: ...impressive.
			2: Defeating my mechanical body...
			3: ...Is not a small feat...
			4: I applaud you, Terrarian.

			5: {
				Normal: Although...next time we meet...when you're stronger...
				Hardcore: I'm also impressed you made it this far in hardcore mode.
			}

			6: {
				Normal: ...{0}...
				Streaming: ...and when there isn't an audiance...

				Hardcore: {
					Normal: Good job, {0}. Here, have a sticker.
					Streaming: Guess an audiance can be pretty motivating. Was this some 'challenge run'? Well here, have a sticker.
				}
			}

			7: {
				Normal: I won't be so forgiving.
				Hardcore: Now, I bid you adieu...
			}
		}

		Second: {
			1: Hmpf...
			2: ...breaking it once wasn't enough for you?
			3: I assume you're doing it for the drops...
			4: ...bragging rights with your friends...perhaps?
			5: Or maybe you get a sick kick out of breaking other people's property.
			6: Who am I to judge, though?
		}

		Third: {
			1: Bravo. You scrapped my body again.
			2: What do you want? A sticker?
			3: A gold star?
			4: I can just remake it again instantly, so I don't get why you keep going after me.
		}

		Fourth: {
			1: Sigh...you are a persistent one, aren't you?
			2: Four times? You must be some kind of masochist or something.
			3: You know, I'm not the aggressor here...
			4: You keep summoning me.
			5: I only showed up because you trashed my Zero unit.
			6: The void wasn't hurting you. It's just there.
			7: You're the one who went in to kill my Zero unit.
			8: Whatever, just take your boss drops and go.
		}

		Tenth: {
			1: {
				Normal: That's what you get for bothering me TEN TIMES.
				Hardcore: I would kill you to teach you a lesson...
			}

			2: {
				Normal: ...but I doubt you'll go away.
				Hardcore: ...but you're in hardcore mode, and I'm not that much of an asshole.
			}

			3: Oh well.
			Kill: "{0} was destroyed by Oblivion"
		}

		Other: {
			1: "{0} kills...congratulations. You have no life."

			2: {
				0: {
					Default: Go outside and kick a ball or something.

					Friends: {
						Online: Why not play something with {0}? They're online right now. Surely playing with them would be more fun than bothering me.
						Offline: Hm, none of your friends are online... Surely you can get one of them to play with you though. Maybe {0}? Or maybe they're all avoiding you... I can see why they might.
						Friendless: Wait, you seriously have zero steam friends?? Wow, maybe you really don't have anything better to do than bother me...
					}
				}

				1: {
					Default: Isn't there some schoolwork you have to do or an application you need to fill out or something?
					Job: Here, let me do you a favor. This is just what you need!
				}

				2: {
					1: Don't you have other games on Steam you could be playing right now?

					Games: {
						Portal2: How about Portal 2? Go annoy GLaDOS some more instead of me.
						StardewValley: Maybe Stardew Valley? Wouldn't your time be better spent tending to your farm than bothering me.
						HollowKnight: You could dive back into Hollow Knight. Leave this Void alone for a bit and deal with that one?
						DontStarve: Perhaps Don't Starve? Deerclops was fun, right? Plenty more fun to be had where that guy came from.
						RoR2: Risk of Rain 2 always has more you could do. Isn't there a Void there you could go bother instead of this one?
						TBoI: The Binding of Issac could be fun, right? Though you spend enough time in the basement as is, huh?
						Minecraft: I bet a bit of Minecraft would do you some good. Do some building instead of destroying for a change?

						Undertale: {
							Normal: You know, how about Undertale? I bet that Skeleton could keep you busy for a while.
							Erased: You know, how about Undertale? Wait, what? Where'd it go? I could have sworn it was...
							Sold: You know, how about Undertale? Hm? Not appealing? Guess you've had your fun with that one, huh.
						}

						Deltarune: Deltarune could be fun. I bet that Knight could keep you entertained a while. Or maybe an egg hunt'll keep you busy?
						Celeste: How about Celeste? Get lost in the mountains for a while? I'd certainly appreciate that.
						Subnautica: Subnautica would be perfect for you. You'll be lost at sea so I'll never have to see you again!
						Ultrakill: Bet Ultrakill is the fix you're looking for. You just love tearing everything you see apart, right?
						DeadCells: Dead Cells could keep you busy right? Aren't some of their trinkets gonna be showing up here soon...?
						DeepRock: Deeprock Galatic could work. Yeah, go dig yourself a hole far, far away. Get some rock and stone and all that.
						DDLC: Oh, that's right. Monika was asking for you wasn't she? Yeah, she misses you a whole lot. You should pay her a visit.
						LethalCompany: Lethal Company would be good, right? Or, no, I guess not. You need friends to play that one.
						TheStanleyParable: Can't you go back to the Stanley Parable? Go bother that Narrator instead of me?
						Bonelords: Oh dude, you have Bonelords? Fuck yeah. Wanna play some Bonelords? Hop on Bonelords after this? ...No?

						SecondStellar: {
							TsaEnabled: Like... Woah man, seriously...? Second Stellar? You REALLY must like that starfarer of yours, huh?
							Normal: Like... Huh, 'Second Stellar'? Do I recognize those two from somewhere?
						}

						Default: {
							Recent: {
								0: Some more {0} would be fun right? You had fun last time, didn't you?
								1: It hasn't been too long since you last played {0}. Go play more of that.
								2: How about {0}? It hasn't been that long.
								3: You've been playing {0} recently, right? Wouldn't that be more fun than bothering me?
							}

							Old: {
								0: Its been a bit. How about {0}? That'd be fun, right?
								1: "{0} looks fun. Go play that."
								2: How about {0}? That'd be fun, right? Play that instead.
								3: You're a fan of {0}, right? Wouldn't that be more fun than bothering me?
							}
						}
					}
				}

				3: {
					Default: Now leave me alone, I have better things to do.
					Computer: If you keep this up I might just have to fry your beloved '{0}'. Don't test me.
				}

				4: {
					Default: Fighting you gets really boring you know. You use the same tactics every time.
					Notification: Message: You should be more careful who you mess with.
				}

				5: {
					Default: Whatever, I'll be seeing you soon...again...assuming you're still a persistent wretch.

					Discord: {
						Server: {
							CalDev: Why are you even fighting me? Don't you have a Sunken Sea Overhaul to be working on or something?
							Default: Why don't you just go back to {0} and find someone to bother there, alright?
						}

						DM: Can't you just go back to bothering {0}? They seem to be willing to put up with you.
					}
				}

				Mods: {
					Thorium: You know Ragnarok is a thing right? World-ending trio? They should be fun to fight. Now go away.
					CalamityMod: Go fight Supreme Calamitas or something. I'm sure she'll occupy your time.
					GRealm: Why don't you go fight the Horde for the 50th goddamn time. Maybe they have new drops or something since you last checked.
					Redemption: If you have such a hardon for killing robots, the Vlitch are a thing, you know.
					SpiritClassic: Why don't you go frolic in the spirit biome. I'm sure one of the creatures there would love a big ol' hug.
					SacredTools: Go bug the Lunarians or something. I'm sure they'll be more fun to fight than I am.
					Tremor: Wait you're playing Tremor? HAHAHAHAHAHAH!
					Fargo: Hey, why not go bug the mutant. If you like killing bosses so much, he should be able to fix you right up.
					NoMod: Go install another mod or something. There are plenty on the mod browser to choose from.
					#New Additions
					Jetshift: Can't you go bother those two meteor guys?
					StarsAbove: Go bother Tsukiyomi, or just go chat with your starfarer friend instead of bothering me.
					LunarVeil: You know Gothiva right? Go fight her. I hear she's tough.
					Catalyst: Why not pummel that Astrageldon thing again? I hear if you no-hit it you can get a special drop.
					CalamityHunt: How about that Goozma thing? You should go fight that thing. It can probably keep you entertained.
					Split: Why don't you go bother Seth again. He has that Ultimate version of himself, right?
					Macrocosm: You can literally go to the Moon. Isn't there more interesting stuff there?
					Spooky: Go dig around those catacombs some more. I'm sure there's something for you to fight in there.
					Ultranium: Why not fight the Abyssal Armageddon again? Isn't it supposed to do something cool during a Blood Moon...?
					YouBoss: Can't you keep yourself occupied? like, literally, with that mirror guy.
					Radiance: Doesn't that sun fairy have some new tricks? Go fight her instead.
					Fables: Why not pay that nautilus pal of yours another visit? He actually likes fighting you.
				}
			}
